     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":3,\"rationale\":\"Block fileServer:lateralMovement, rdpLogin:authenticate and hypervisor:privilegeEscalation. (1) Blocking fileServer stops codeRepo, since its other parent secretsManager is an AND that needs fileServer. That also stops vaultRead, which depends only on secretsManager. (2) Blocking rdpLogin stops domainAdmin, an AND. That removes mailArchive and one of dbReplica's parents. (3) Blocking hypervisor removes dbReplica's last live parent. Two blocks are not enough because the target has three independent routes. Route A is tokenCache to fileServer to codeRepo, and tokenCache is fed directly by footholds. Route B is apiToken plus rdpLogin to domainAdmin to mailArchive. Route C is printServer and monitoringHost to hypervisor to dbReplica, fed via dbLogin and configSecret. No single blockable step lies on two of these routes. The closest candidate is containerHost:execution, which feeds apiToken and vpnSession. Blocking it still leaves hypervisor reachable via dbLogin, and codeRepo reachable via tokenCache.\"}"
    }
   ],
